classi-fly NOTICE
=================

This repository ships a runtime and CLI that operate on `.fly` classifier
artifacts. Artifacts built from third-party data carry their source's
license and attribution in the artifact header (`license`, `attribution`
fields). The following sources are used by the offline tooling:

1. Hemibrain connectome (Janelia FlyEM, Drosophila melanogaster adult brain)
   License: CC-BY 4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International).
   Source: FlyEM Hemibrain release, Janelia Research Campus
   (https://www.janelia.org/project-team/flyem/hemibrain).
   Required attribution when shipping an artifact derived from it:
   "Hemibrain: Scheffer et al. 2020, eLife 9:e57443" (adjust to the exact
   citation of the version used).

2. Larval connectome (Drosophila melanogaster larval brain, Winding 2023)
   License: CC BY 4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International).
   Source: Winding et al. 2023, Science 379:eadd9330.
   Required attribution when shipping an artifact derived from it:
   "Winding et al. 2023, Science 379:eadd9330".

3. Synthetic reservoirs (seed-generated via tools/ingest/synthetic.py)
   License: none. No third-party data. The default shippable artifact.

FlyWire-derived data (FAFB, BANC, MCNS, MANC) is licensed CC BY-NC 4.0
(non-commercial). The `classi-fly pack` command refuses to ship it without
an explicit `--allow-noncommercial` flag; artifacts produced that way are
for benchmark and research use only and must not be used commercially.

